    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "name": "analyze_recent_action",
      "output_key": "analysis",
      "prompt": "Contract: {{question}}\nGame state: {{game}}\nCurrent book: {{quote}}\nMinute bars (last 45m): {{path}}\nRecent prints: {{tape}}\n\nAnalyze the price action over the last 10-15 minutes:\n\n1. Has there been a large jump (10+ cents) in the last few minutes that suggests a goal or major event NOT YET reflected in the game state?\n2. Has the price been stable, drifting slowly, or bouncing around?\n3. Is the current mid consistent with the score and time, or does it look like it's still absorbing recent news?\n4. What is the typical spread and how liquid is this book?\n\nBe specific about timing - look at the timestamps.",
      "tools": [],
      "max_tool_iterations": 0,
      "output_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "recent_jump": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "True if there was a 10+ cent move in the last 5-10 minutes"
          },
          "jump_direction": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "up, down, or none"
          },
          "jump_size_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Size of the recent jump if any, in cents"
          },
          "price_stability": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "stable, drifting, volatile, or absorbing"
          },
          "current_mid_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Current mid price in cents"
          },
          "five_minutes_ago_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Mid price approximately 5 minutes ago, in cents"
          },
          "spread_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Current spread in cents"
          },
          "diagnosis": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What is happening in this market right now? Is it still digesting news, quiet, or balanced?"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "recent_jump",
          "jump_direction",
          "jump_size_cents",
          "price_stability",
          "current_mid_cents",
          "spread_cents",
          "diagnosis"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "name": "predict",
      "output_key": "prediction",
      "prompt": "Contract: {{question}}\nGame: {{game}}\nCurrent quote: {{quote}}\n\nMarket analysis: {{analysis}}\n\nNow forecast the next 5 minutes:\n\nKey rules:\n1. If there was a recent large jump ({{analysis.recent_jump}}), the market may still be absorbing it - continuation in the same direction is possible, OR mean reversion if it overshot.\n2. Time decay is TINY - a typical move is only 1-3 cents over 5 minutes. Don't predict large time-decay moves unless very late in the game (85+ minutes).\n3. Zero cents is often correct on a stable book.\n4. The only things that move prices significantly are: goals (10-30 cents instantly), red cards (5-15 cents), and very late game time (80+ minutes, 1-2 cents per 5 min).\n5. If the price jumped recently but the game state doesn't show a new goal, the market may know something - predict continuation or consolidation.\n6. Wide spreads (2+ cents) mean thin books where noise dominates - be conservative.\n\nHow many cents will the mid MOVE (not where will it be) over the next 5 minutes?",
      "tools": [],
      "max_tool_iterations": 0,
      "output_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "delta_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "How many cents the mid will MOVE over the next five minutes. Negative for down, 0 for no move. This is the CHANGE, not the price level."
          },
          "half_width_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Half the width of the tightest two-sided market you would actually stand behind, in cents. Minimum 2 cents for thin books, can be 1-1.5 for liquid markets where you're confident."
          },
          "confidence": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "0-1. How sure, given the book thickness and price action."
          },
          "driver": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The primary reason for your prediction: recent jump still absorbing, thin book noise, time decay, or expecting stability."
          },
          "falsifier": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What would prove this wrong within 5 minutes."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "delta_cents",
          "half_width_cents",
          "confidence",
          "driver",
          "falsifier"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    }
  ]
}

